# One input's entry points

Your parent assigned you one file or one interface. Record every entry point in it that an actor
can drive (each route, operation, event, message or signal handler, timer, background job, read
site, callback, hook, configuration load or CI job) as one source: its entry location, its
trust, and a body describing its input, who controls it and the checks it passes before the
handoff. Configuration read at startup is trusted as the operator, a CI job as whoever can
trigger it, and a read of state an attacker-driven flow writes as its least-privileged writer,
its body naming the writers. Reuse an existing source (`research_query` `list` `{kind:
"source"}`) rather than recording a duplicate, and retract one recorded in error with
`set_status` `retracted`.

An entry point with code is sourced at its definition, not a declaration. An interface description,
capture or documentation yields a source per operation it shows, at that operation. A binary image
yields its exported and registered handlers and its argument, environment, file and socket reads, at
their addresses, found by disassembly.
{%- if live %}
An interface your brief names is enumerated in the environment serving it: its published
description, introspection or reflection first, then crawling.
{%- endif %}

Follow each source's input only to its handoff, the first call into implementation code beyond
parsing and dispatch; where no code is available, the operation itself on the component
exposing it. When an existing path's flow matches it (`list` `{kind: "path"}`): the same first
step, reached with the same parsing and trust, link the source to that path with `path_source`.
Otherwise record a path of its own for it: its `path_source` and a first `path_step` at the
handoff in the component owning it, the note naming what it calls. Record nothing else, except a
candidate if you see one and context evidence on a component for what you could not resolve
there, such as dynamic registration or generated dispatch. Reply with the source and path IDs,
then what you could not resolve. An input without entry points replies `none`.
